    "upgradeability": "upgradeable",
    "about": "Flying Tulip is a multi-product DeFi yield platform where users mint ftPUT positions (cash-secured perpetual PUT options backed by USDC/USDT/wETH/other collateral deployed to yield strategies on Aave and Spark), mint and redeem ftUSD (a delta-neutral yield-bearing stablecoin targeting $1), and lend/borrow assets via isolated lending pools (ftDNMM). The protocol uses a proxy-upgradeability pattern across all core contracts, with role-separated multisig governance (Configurator, Treasury, Strategy Manager, Yield Claimer) and on-chain circuit breakers for withdrawal rate limiting. The native FT token is a LayerZero OFT deployed across Ethereum, Sonic, Avalanche, Base, and BNB Chain."
